    "https://www.unh.edu/career/employers": {
      "title": "Employers",
      "description": "Employers | Career and Professional Success Skip to main content University of New Hampshire Search Menu Search UNH.edu Search Career and Professional Success Search UNH.edu Search Search Commonly Searched Items: Handshake Wildcat Connections Career Events Career and Professional Success Students Make an Appointment Resources Jobs and Careers for Students Internships Internship Funding Opportunities Applying to Grad School Reserve an Interview Room Employers Recruiting Opportunities Partnerships & Sponsorships Submit Recruiting Survey Handshake for Employers Explore Internship Resources Become a Work Study Site Hire a UNH Law Student Review Policies Career Technology Handshake for Students Workday On-Campus Employment Generative AI for Career Handshake for Volunteer Organizations Forage Career Events Career & Internship Fair Interview Days Industry-Specific Career Events Career Event Student Preparation Alumni Career Resources for Alumni Faculty & Staff Handshake for UNH Departments CaPS Information and Partnership Opportunities Faculty & Staff Employer Visit Request Resources for Advising Students About CaPS Meet the CaPS Team First Destination Survey Student Experience Survey Campus-2-Career Employers Employers Advertise Positions on Handshake for Employers Explore our Recruiting Opportunities Expand Brand Marketing through Sponsorship Understand our Recruiting Policies Register for a Career Event Career and Professional Success connects employers to talented and hardworking students from all majors and degree levels for employment, internships and recruiting opportunities Connect with Our Team Through our Recruiting Survey About the University The University of New Hampshire is the state’s flagship public research university, providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate programs and graduate programs of distinction. From its main campus in Durham, campus in Manchester , online programs and the UNH School of Law in Concord , the university serves New Hampshire and the world through continuing education, Cooperative Extension , cultural outreach, economic development and applied research. 200+ Degree Programs 13,000+ Undergraduate Students 2,400+ Graduate Students CLASSIFIED AS AN R1 CATEGORY BY THE CARNEGIE CLASSIFICATION OF INSTITUTIONS OF HIGHER EDUCATION Did You Know? UNH is a Land, Sea and Space Grant university. Over 1,800 UNH undergraduate students, from all academic disciplines, present annually at the URC. The presentations showcase the results of students’ research, scholarly, and creative projects in over 20 professional and artistic venues at both campuses (Durham and Manchester), making the UNH URC one of the largest conferences of its kind in the country. 20% Students travel abroad 70 countries represented 250+ Clubs and organizations 3.5 Average enrolling GPA Highest Enrolled Bachelor's Degree Programs Business Administration Undeclared Liberal Arts Psychology Biomedical Science Mechanical Engineering Communication English Civil Engineering Undeclared Paul Political Science Explore all majors here Colleges College of Engineering and Physical Sciences College of Health and Human Services College of Life Sciences & Agriculture Peter T. Paul College of Business & Economics College of Professional Studies College of Liberal Arts Recent Success Stories UNH to Host Inaugural Northeast Space, Technology, Trade, and Research Expo in October Event will connect industry, research, students throughout N.H.’s space ecosystem Thursday, August 20, 2026 What Can You Do with a Master's in Community Development? One CEO's Answer Thursday, August 13, 2026 The Hidden Costs of College: What Adult Learners Should Compare Beyond Tuition Looking Beyond the Sticker Price Tuesday, June 30, 2026 The Next Step Handshake Schedule an Appointment Reserve an Interview Room Hire a Wildcat CAPS by college College of Engineering and Physical Sciences College of Health and Human Services College of Liberal Arts Colle